        "ruleId": "nutr.pal.table",
        "note": "BU PAL values leave out resistance training (that is costed separately) and run 1.00–1.48. ClientIntake uses 1.2–1.725, which double-counts training on top of the training-day expenditure."
      },
      {
        "ruleId": "nutr.energy.factor",
        "note": "BU scales the surplus by training status (beginner 5–15%, intermediate 2–7%, advanced 1–3%) and the deficit by leanness (about 2.5–7.5% near contest leanness up to 30–50% at high body fat). ClientIntake uses a fixed factor per goal: 0.8 cut, 1.0 maintain, 1.1 build."
      },
      {
        "ruleId": "safety.deficit.max",
        "note": "BU allows deficits of 30–50% at higher body fat (and up to 30% early in a lean prep). The 25% safety cap is stricter. That may be intended as a safety margin, but BU does not state it."
      }
    ],
